        "id": 1136354
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-10T21:24:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Jeff! I am not sure it is a convention to put a pointer (*PythonVersionProperties) in our properties struct (since it is usually user specific) for our programming convenience.  I think it might be good to keep properties struct as clean as possible. And if we put the pointer there I suspect that user might have access to it. And another thing is that when the module does a second, or third time module split, the creation of variations will not just do a copy of the pointer value but also a deep copy for the content the pointer originally points to. So I am also concerned about that might consume some unnecessary memories.\n\nLet\u0027s wait Dan and Colin to see if they have some opinions",
      "parentUuid": "c53f80cb_33e60473",
      "revId": "aefd2e859d04084c9ee4ce3eca4f32a1f57ac1c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
